"""gen_launcher_batch4.py — derive launchers/launch_qa_secuura_batch1038_1041.sh from launchers/launch_qa_secuura_ks1101_1037.sh (the api-gateway
tier 1 launcher) by ASSERTED block substitutions: every anchor must occur exactly as often as stated, or the generator refuses and writes nothing.

ONE BATCHED gate, TIER 1 floor, FOUR PRs: #1038 KS-1233, #1039 KS-1248, #1040 KS-1125, #1041 KS-1209. The template checks ONE head; the head check, the
compare and the JUDGED set are therefore REPLACED as blocks with per-PR loops (four heads, four compares, one JUDGED table carrying all four PRs' files).
Pins are RE-READ from the repo: every PR's parent must BE develop 207716440, every PR file must equal its CANONICAL local-model patch (re-applied here in
a scratch index), the four must be pairwise file-disjoint, and every merge (each PR over develop; each PR over a SIMULATED develop+#922 squash; all four
together) must be clean — all re-derived read-only in a throwaway bare repo whose objects/info/alternates points at the checkout (left in place).

#922 IS SIGNED TO MERGE and develop is expected to move under this gate. Its squash touches packages/shared/src (fixtures.ts, the ks256 test), which is
GUARDED here because api-gateway imports @secuura/shared. DEV_CONTENT_ALLOWED therefore clears EXACTLY #922's round-2 blobs of those two files and
nothing else: a develop carrying #922 passes, a develop carrying any other shared edit refuses (exit 18).
Usage: gen_launcher_batch4.py <template launcher> <output launcher>   Exit: 0 written · 1 anchor/control/pin disagreed · 2 residual token · 3 bash -n"""
