# ABSENT; any PR's head blob -> exit 19 LANDED, naming the PR), and what the gate runs: startup-migrations.ts (the KS-1125 tamper target), index.ts,
# admin.ts / verification.ts / health.ts (the platform-settings readers), the gateway package.json / vitest.config.ts / vitest.setup.ts / tsconfig.json,
# eslint.config.mjs, the four preflight sibling suites and .githooks/pre-push (which invokes preflight.sh). GUARDED: services/api-gateway/src/ + its
# config, packages/shared/src/, scripts/preflight/, scripts/__tests__/, .githooks/, eslint.config.mjs.
#
# SOURCE = gatesets/2026-09-18_gate1038to1041/mail_batch4_ready.md, the seat's READY mail captured verbatim by message id from wednesday-agent@.
#
# exit 6:  any of the four heads is not at its branch on origin (the refusal names the PR).
# exit 7:  the prompt must carry the TIER 1 floor AND each PR's own tier line.
# exit 20: the READY mail AND the prompt must name all four heads.
